Subject: [PATCH 6/6] cmake: build the post office's POSIX socket backend under Emscripten

ext/aemu_postoffice/client/postoffice.c is compiled unconditionally and calls
into whichever sock_impl_*.c the platform list selects. Emscripten sets UNIX but
not LINUX, so it selected none, and the link ended in

    wasm-ld: error: lib/libCore.a(postoffice.c.o): undefined symbol:
             native_close_tcp_sock

and a dozen more like it.

Emscripten's libc is musl-derived and it has the BSD sockets API, so the POSIX
backend is the correct one rather than merely the one that compiles. What a
browser actually does with a TCP connect is a separate question from whether
this links; ad-hoc multiplayer needs a relay either way.

Needs the SO_NOSIGPIPE fix in the aemu_postoffice submodule — see
native/patches/submodules/.

diff --git a/Core/CMakeLists.txt b/Core/CMakeLists.txt
index 3c902b2ff..c543a496c 100644
--- a/Core/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Core/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -13,7 +13,13 @@ if(WIN32)
 	)
 endif()
 
-if(LINUX OR ANDROID OR MACOSX OR IOS OR BSD)
+# EMSCRIPTEN is in this list because postoffice.c is compiled unconditionally and
+# calls into whichever sock_impl_*.c the platform selects. Emscripten sets UNIX but
+# not LINUX, so without it the post office compiles and then fails to link with
+# native_close_tcp_sock and friends undefined. Its libc is musl-derived and it has
+# the BSD sockets API, so the POSIX backend is the right one — what a browser does
+# with a TCP connect is a separate question from whether this links.
+if(LINUX OR ANDROID OR MACOSX OR IOS OR BSD OR EMSCRIPTEN)
 	list(APPEND aemu_postoffice
 		${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/ext/aemu_postoffice/client/sock_impl_linux.c
 	)
